      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Genus-level entry; species differ (A. macrorrhizos, A. amazonica and others). Watering conflict: NC State keep consistently moist, RHS water once the upper 5 cm has dried (April to October) and barely in winter; kept keep_moist per rule 5. Winter dormancy is described by RHS and NC State but with no number, so rest factor stays unknown. Temperature is NC State daytime 68 to 77 F; RHS says keep above 16 C and never below 10 C in winter. Size varies from 0.5 to 4.5 m by species: unknown. Severity 2: NC State rates the poison medium, ASPCA lists dogs and cats as toxic. NC State also lists eye injury (no eye symptom in our vocabulary, not graded) and says it can be fatal in serious cases; gloves advised (RHS)."
      },
